     "content": "### 1. Is this a good offer?\n\n**Yes, it is a competitive baseline offer for Google L6 PM in San Francisco, but you should not accept it as-is.**\n\nBecause you were passively recruited and are happy in your current role at Meta, you hold significant leverage. \n\n---\n\n### 2. Detailed Compensation Breakdown\n\nTo evaluate this accurately, you must account for **Google\u2019s front-loaded RSU vesting schedule**. \n\nUnlike Meta (which typically vests equity evenly at 25%/year or quarterly in equal tranches), Google\u2019s standard initial new-hire grant vests **33% in Year 1, 33% in Year 2, 22% in Year 3, and 12% in Year 4**.\n\n```\nGoogle Offer ($1.08M RSUs @ 33 / 33 / 22 / 12)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Year 1: $235k Base + $47k Bonus + $356.4k Equity = ~$638,400\n\u2022 Year 2: $235k Base + $47k Bonus + $356.4k Equity = ~$638,400\n\u2022 Year 3: $235k Base + $47k Bonus + $237.6k Equity = ~$519,600 (+ Refresher 1)\n\u2022 Year 4: $235k Base + $47k Bonus + $129.6k Equity = ~$411,600 (+ Refreshers 1 & 2)\n```\n\n#### Comparison vs. Meta:\n* **Years 1 & 2:** You get an immediate cash-flow bump of **+$112k/year** over your current Meta comp ($526k/yr).\n* **Years 3 & 4 (The \"Vesting Cliff\"):** Your initial grant drops sharply. Google expects annual performance refreshers (which vest over 4 years, typically 25%/yr) to stack and fill this gap. If your performance rating is average, your comp in Years 3 and 4 could dip close to or below your current Meta rate.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Weaknesses in the Current Offer\n\n1. **Base Salary is a Step Down:** Offered at **$235,000**, which is lower than your current **$240,000** at Meta, and well below Google's posted band maximum of **$271,000**.\n2. **Zero Sign-on Bonus:** Leaving unvested Meta equity ($200k in the next 12 months) and a stable team deserves a buyout/sign-on component. At L6, sign-on bonuses of **$50,000\u2013$100,000+** are standard.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Should You Accept, Negotiate, or Walk Away?\n\n* **Do not accept right away.** You have not left anything on the table yet.\n* **Do not walk away.** The compensation baseline and level calibration (Meta IC6 $\\rightarrow$ Google L6) are solid.\n* **Negotiate.** You have the strongest possible profile for negotiation: strong current performance, no pressure to move, and high unvested equity.\n\n---\n\n### 5. What to Ask For (Your Counter-Offer)\n\nAim to push the total package value to the top of Google's L6 band by targeting three specific levers:\n\n| Component | Initial Offer | What to Counter With | Rationale |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $235,000 | **$255,000 \u2013 $260,000** | Exceeds your current Meta base ($240k) while remaining comfortably within the posted band cap ($271k). |\n| **New-Hire RSUs** | $1,080,000 / 4 yrs | **$1,200,000 \u2013 $1,250,000 / 4 yrs** | Protects against the Year 3/4 cliff and matches top-of-market L6 PM offers. |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$75,000 \u2013 $100,000** | Offsets your upcoming Meta vesting tranches and lost bonus cycle. |\n\n---\n\n### 6. Suggested Negotiation Script / Framing\n\nWhen speaking with the recruiter, remain warm, excited, and grounded in your numbers:\n\n> *\"Thank you for putting this offer together. I\u2019ve really enjoyed meeting the team, and I\u2019m genuinely excited about the scope of the role.*\n>\n> *As I mentioned early on, I wasn\u2019t actively looking to leave Meta, where I'm performing well and tracking around $526k in total compensation with $240k base and significant unvested equity over the next 12 months.*\n>\n> *To make the move an easy decision, I\u2019m looking for a package that clearly reflects that step up across all components:*\n> 1. *A base salary of **$255,000** (to avoid taking a step back on fixed cash).*\n> 2. *An equity grant of **$1,200,000** over 4 years to bridge the long-term cliff.*\n> 3. *A sign-on bonus of **$75,000\u2013$100,000** to help offset unvested Meta RSUs and bonus timing.*\n>\n> *If we can get close to these numbers, I\u2019d be thrilled to sign and give my notice.\"*",
