     "content": "**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nThis is an exceptional outcome for a Google L6 Product Manager negotiation. Securing a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** on top of a **$1.08M RSU grant** and a matched **$240k base** pushes this package to the very top percentile for L6 compensation in the Bay Area.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Updated Numbers\n\nUsing Google\u2019s front-loaded vesting schedule (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**):\n\n```\nGoogle Final Offer Breakdown\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Year 1: $240k Base + $48k Bonus + $356.4k RSUs + $200k Sign-on = ~$844,400\n\u2022 Year 2: $240k Base + $48k Bonus + $356.4k RSUs                  = ~$644,400\n\u2022 Year 3: $240k Base + $48k Bonus + $237.6k RSUs (+ Refreshers)   = ~$525,600+\n\u2022 Year 4: $240k Base + $48k Bonus + $129.6k RSUs (+ Refreshers)   = ~$417,600+\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n4-Year Minimum Baseline Total: ~$2,432,000 (~$608,000 / year avg)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. How This Compares to Staying at Meta\n\n* **2-Year Comparison:**\n  * **Meta (2 Years):** ~$1,052,000\n  * **Google (2 Years):** ~$1,488,800\n  * **Difference:** You gain nearly **+$440,000 in additional cash/equity** over your first 24 months.\n* **Risk Mitigation:** The $200k sign-on fully liquidates your unvested Meta risk immediately on day one, without having to wait out the next 12 months of vesting tranches.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Why You Shouldn't Push Further on Money\n\nWhen a tech recruiter says *\"this is our best offer\"* after granting a $200k sign-on and lifting base salary:\n1. They had to go to compensation committee/VP-level approval to get an off-band exception for that sign-on bonus.\n2. Pushing again without a competing written counter-offer risks exhausting goodwill before you even start with your hiring manager.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\nBefore returning the signed paperwork, check two administrative details with the recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-on Bonus Schedule & Clawback:**\n   * Is the $200,000 paid as a lump sum on your first or second paycheck, or split across Year 1 and Year 2?\n   * Verify the clawback period (standard is a 1-year or 2-year pro-rated repayment if you leave voluntarily).\n2. **Start Date Timing:**\n   * Align your start date to ensure you don\u2019t leave Meta right before a quarterly vesting date or bonus payout window if one is imminent.\n\n---\n\n### Final Verdict\n\nFrom a financial standpoint, this is a clear win. Assuming you like the team, product domain, and manager at Google, **sign the offer.**",
